IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `hsa-charges`
IMPORT `hsa-qa`

-- Health Services Act 2016 (WA), with the Health Services (Fees and Charges) Order 2016 -- cases for the Q&A layer
-- (hsa-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the answer
-- must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation ("it is an assumed term").
-- Each question that takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with each value under which the situation does
-- not hold, every later input ASSUMEd. For the patient (the baseline's seat), cases check that the answer equals the
-- baseline export's on the same facts, built here as the baseline's own `Me as a patient` record; a charge question, which
-- takes the patient's class, is given the class the baseline works out from that record, and the cases check that the
-- patient the layer builds for each class has that class. Expected values are worked by hand from the Act and the Order
-- (figures in force from 1 July 2026).
--
-- Facts from the WA lives: Chloe's antenatal care and birth (c060), Jake's three weeks after a stroke (k090). The other
-- cases are illustrative.
--
-- Written by the scratchpad script gen_hsa_cases.py, which only spells out the argument lists.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked election` IS A `My election`
ASSUME `an unasked attendance` IS A `How I attend`
ASSUME `an unasked bed` IS A `My bed`
ASSUME `an unasked provider` IS A `Who provides my health service`
ASSUME `an unasked concession` IS A `My medicine concession`
ASSUME `an unasked study` IS A `My MRI study`
ASSUME `an unasked way of fixing` IS A `How my charge is fixed`
ASSUME `an unasked kind of payment` IS A `Kind of payment`
ASSUME `an unasked reason` IS A `Why my information is disclosed`
ASSUME `an unasked reason for staying` IS A `Why I am staying with the patient`
ASSUME `an unasked reason of mine` IS A `Why I would use or disclose it`
ASSUME `an unasked compensation` IS A `My compensation position`
ASSUME `an unasked class` IS A `My class`

`as the patient` MEANS `I am a patient of a WA public health service`
`as the family member` MEANS `I am a family member or carer of a patient, or stay in hospital with one`
`as the payer` MEANS `I must pay compensation to someone a public hospital treated for their injury`
`as the holder` MEANS `I hold information about someone that I obtained through the WA health system`

-- The baseline's own records, for the cases that compare with the baseline export.
`a Medicare-eligible public patient` MEANS `Me as a patient` WITH
    `I am an eligible person under the Health Insurance Act 1973` IS TRUE
    `I have, or appear to have, a right to compensation for this condition` IS FALSE
    `the chief executive has decided I am not a compensable patient` IS FALSE
    `motor vehicle third party insurance applies or appears to apply` IS FALSE
    `workers compensation, catastrophic injuries or Defence Force law applies or appears to apply` IS FALSE
    `I am a veteran who elects the DVA arrangement` IS FALSE
    `I am a nursing home type patient` IS FALSE
    `my election` IS `to be a public patient`
    `I am an asylum seeker` IS FALSE
    `I am an involuntary patient under the Mental Health Act 2014` IS FALSE
    `the service is part of my Mental Health Act treatment` IS FALSE
    `a declaration under s 6(2) of the Health Insurance Act 1973 applies to me` IS FALSE

